  "body": "## Summary\n\nWhen a `thread_title` request also offers a function tool, the upstream can answer with a tool call, but `codexTitle` drops that call and returns only message text. A Codex title hook can therefore see `set_thread_title` never invoked, even though the tool was sent and the model chose it.\n\nThis is not specific to `set_thread_title`: any function tool offered on a title request is lost in the same way.\n\n## Reproduce\n\nUsing Codex app-server against magpie as the provider:\n\n1. Start an ephemeral thread with `threadSource: \"thread_title\"`.\n2. Pass a dynamic function tool named `set_thread_title` with a small schema.\n3. Start a turn whose prompt asks the model to call that tool.\n\nObserved: the model responds with a tool call, but no `item/tool/call` reaches the client; with a normal `threadSource: \"user\"` request on the same daemon and model, the tool call arrives immediately.\n\nI also see this at the gateway level: an upstream Chat response with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"choices\": [{\n    \"delta\": {\n      \"tool_calls\": [{\n        \"index\": 0,\n        \"id\": \"call_1\",\n        \"type\": \"function\",\n        \"function\": {\n          \"name\": \"set_thread_title\",\n          \"arguments\": \"{\\\"title\\\":\\\"...\\\"}\"\n        }\n      }]\n    },\n    \"finish_reason\": \"tool_calls\"\n  }]\n}\n```\n\nis turned by `codexTitle` into a `response.completed` whose `output` has only the extracted message title; no `function_call` item is preserved.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`internal/gateway/codex_titles.go`, `(*Server).codexTitle`:\n\n```go\nvar out []any\nif t := titleJSON(messageText(res), shape); t != \"\" {\n    out = append(out, map[string]any{\"type\": \"message\", ...})\n} else if res.Status == \"incomplete\" {\n    ...\n}\nwriteTitleReply(w, id, out, res.Usage)\n```\n\n`messageText(res)` only reads `compactOutput.Type == \"message\"` (`internal/gateway/codex_titles.go`, `messageText`). `compactReply` already decodes a `function_call` into `res.Output`, but `codexTitle` never forwards it; `compactOutput` also currently drops `call_id` and `arguments` while decoding, so even a forwarding fix needs those fields retained.\n\nThis differs from a normal turn: `responses.go`'s encoder turns `ToolCall` into a `function_call` item. The title handler rebuilds the response by hand instead.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nA title hook may legitimately want the title model to call a tool (for example `set_thread_title`) instead of only emitting text. With the current wrapper, the call is silently discarded. The title model can still be selected through `thread_title`, but tool-based title workflows cannot complete and look like a model failure.\n\n## Suggested minimal fix\n\n1. Add `CallID` and `Arguments` to `compactOutput` so `compactReply` retains a decoded call.\n2. In `codexTitle`, if the upstream output contains a function call, forward it as a Responses `function_call` item rather than converting it to a text title. Preserve the call's `call_id`, `name`, and `arguments`; generate an item id using the existing `itemPrefix`/`newID` conventions.\n3. Keep the current text-title path unchanged when no call is present.\n\nAn alternative, if title requests should remain text-only by design, is to explicitly reject or surface tool calls as a title failure rather than silently dropping them. I'd prefer the first because it makes the route composable and keeps compatibility with existing text-only titles.\n\n## Test suggestions\n\n- A `thread_title` request with a function tool and an upstream `tool_calls` reply returns a `function_call` item with the same `call_id`, `name`, and `arguments`.\n- The existing text-only title tests still return `{\"title\":\"...\"}`.\n- A title request whose upstream returns both `message` and `function_call` has a deterministic, documented precedence.\n\n## Environment\n\n- magpie `v0.1.2140-855-ga3768cdd1` (checked against current `origin/main`, `a3768cdd1`)\n- macOS Apple Silicon\n- Codex desktop app-server, ephemeral `thread_title` thread\n- Provider: a Chat-Completions-backed titling model\n\nI tested this through a local Codex title hook, not by changing magpie source. I have not opened a PR; this issue records the reproduction and the smallest source-level fix I can see.\n",
