   "body": "Reproduced and fixed on a fork branch: `fix/4942-title-function-call` (skygunner/magpie, head `2880d2df8`, based on `main` at `8abdf53a8`).\n\n**Root cause**\n\n`codexTitle` (`internal/gateway/codex_titles.go`) rebuilds the title reply by hand from the model's text alone: `messageText` reads only `message` items, so a `function_call` in the upstream reply never reached the output — exactly what you saw: a Chat `tool_calls` reply came back as a `response.completed` whose `output` held only the extracted title (or nothing). Two things kept it that way: `compactOutput` (`internal/gateway/codex_backend.go`) dropped `call_id` and `arguments` while decoding, so there was nothing to forward, and the missing-title check flagged the reply as a failed title (\"the model answered with no text\") on top of dropping it.\n\n**Fix**\n\n- `compactOutput` keeps a `function_call`'s `call_id` and `arguments` as `compactReply` decodes it.\n- `codexTitle` forwards every `function_call` of the reply as a Responses `function_call` item — `call_id`, `name`, `arguments` as the model made them, the item id minted through the existing `itemPrefix`/`newID` conventions (`fc_…`, same as a normal turn's encoder writes) — ahead of any text; the text-title path is unchanged when no call is present, and a reply with both is documented as call-first.\n- A reply that called a tool no longer trips the missing-title check, so the turn is not recorded as a failed title in Usage/Routing.\n- One clause added to `docs/subsystems/gateway-routing.md`'s titles section.\n\n**Verification**\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `TestCodexTitleForwardsAFunctionCall` on base `8abdf53a8` | FAIL: output `[]` and the ledger's call failed with \"title: the model answered with no text, so Codex got no title\" |\n| the same with the change | green: `function_call` item with `call_id` `call_1`, `name` `set_thread_title`, `arguments` as sent, `fc_…` item id; the turn not a failure |\n| text-only title tests (`TestCodexTitlesSetting`, `TestCodexTitleOnMagpieProvider`, `TestTitleJSON*`) | green — still `{\"title\": ...}` |\n| title/description/summary/compaction/protection/format-fence batch | 548 pass, 1 red — `TestCodexPoolSaysTheClientsVersion`, pre-existing on bare `main` on this machine (its hardcoded 0.161.0 is older than the installed Codex CLI), green solo |\n| `count=3` on the regression test, `gofmt`, `go vet -tags nogui`, `go build -tags nogui` | pass |\n\n**Not verified**: a real Codex app-server title hook against a live model — no such environment here; the test reproduces your gateway-level capture (the Chat `tool_calls` reply) at the wire level. Descriptions, summaries and predictions keep their text-only wrapping; `custom_tool_call` and hosted-tool items are not forwarded.\n\nThis is a fork branch, ready for review, not a claim on the issue's ownership.\n",
