     "body": "Sibling of #4449. `clientNamedWorkPlace` (Claude bridge) now reads the caller's own layer first (its instructions, its system messages) and a user turn only for the forms a caller states there (Codex's `<environment_context>`, OpenCode's `<env>`).\n\n`workDirIn` / `factsOf` in `internal/gateway/workdir.go` still take the **last** folder named anywhere in the system prompt and every non-assistant text part. A user turn that quotes `Primary working directory: /x` alone on its line therefore:\n\n- picks the routing group rule by folder for that request, and\n- goes to a plugin's provider as `provider.WorkDirHeader` (`tellWorkPlace`), so a plugin tells its vendor the quoted folder, not the agent's.\n\nAlso `CWD: /x` (claude --bare) is not read there.\n\nProposed: read workDirIn in the same two layers as clientNamedWorkPlace (share the patterns), with a test per WardLu's P3 case.",
